<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12094" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybĕlē</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybēbē</span></b> ,
		ēs, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybĕ-lă</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυβέλη</span> and
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυβήβη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A goddess, originally Phrygian, later worshipped in
				Rome also as</i> Ops <i>or</i> Mater Magna, <i>whose priests were called</i> Galli. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> Form Cybele, <i><span class="en">Cat. 63,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 11, 768</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 1,
				71, 10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b> Form Cybela, <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Nat. 1,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			Form Cybebe, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 10, 220</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3,
			17</span></i> (4, 16), 35; <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 3, 17, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			365</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cat.
				63, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 3, 17, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 1, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 1,
			600</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybĕ-lēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., pertaining to
			Cybele</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 104</span></i>
			; v. Attis: mater, i. q. <i>Cybele</i>, <i><span class="en">id. A. A. 1,
				507</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">so also dea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					4, 191</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frena,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of the lions in the chariot of Cybele</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					M. 10, 704</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">limina,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of her temple</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1, 2, 176</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybĕlista</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυβελιστής</span>, <i>a priest of Cybele</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Verg. Copa, 25</span></i> Sillig ex conj.
			(al. Calybita). —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mountain in Phrygia</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> Form Cybele, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4,
				249</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 363</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b> Form Cybebe, <i><span class="en">Cat. 63,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">63,
			84</span></i>.—Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cybĕ-lus</span></b> , i,
				m., <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3, 111</span></i> Rib. (al.
		Cybelae).</div>
